  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "If \\(200 \\le a \\le 400\\) and \\(600 \\le b \\le 1200,\\) then the largest value of the quotient \\(\\dfrac{b}{a}\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac32\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(300\\)",
    "E": "\\(600\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Both quantities are positive, and \\(a\\ge200\\), so the quotient is always defined. A positive fraction increases when its numerator increases or its denominator decreases. Therefore every allowed choice satisfies\n\\[\n\\frac ba\\le\\frac{1200}{a}\\le\\frac{1200}{200}=6.\n\\]\nThe values \\(b=1200\\) and \\(a=200\\) are both allowed, and they give equality. Hence the largest quotient is \\(6\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
